{
  "name": "657. A Runware task delivered async or to a webhook under a dollar budget is refused before the call (runware-deferred) [SERIAL]",
  "description": "TXE-8013 security and billing regression. Local fixture regression: run with providerErrorFixture=1 against the gateway of tests/e2e/api/provider_config/provider-error-fixture.config.json, with tests/e2e/api/runners/provider-error-fixture.mjs as the only upstream. A Runware passthrough task sent with deliveryMethod async, or with a webhookURL, is answered with a queued acknowledgment, and nothing charges the task when it finishes: a webhook result never passes Bifrost, and the getResponse that fetches an async one names no model. Under a dollar budget both are now refused 403 (error_type policy_model_blocked, type background_unsettled) before the upstream call. The same task sent sync passes the deferred-delivery gate and is judged by the price book instead: the fixture prices no Runware model, so it is refused model_unpriced (TXE-7957), which shows the two gates apart. The same rule reaches past Runware: a typed chat on the priced openai/gpt-6-luna that forwards callback_url in its extra params (x-bf-passthrough-extra-params, 657.4), and a passthrough transcription carrying webhook=true as a multipart (657.5) or urlencoded (657.6) form field, are refused background_unsettled. Red before TXE-8013: 657.4 reached the fixture (which answers 404 for a chat on gpt-6-luna) instead of being refused, and 657.5 was not refused background_unsettled. No row reaches the upstream, so the fixture needs no Runware or transcription handler. [SERIAL]: the rows read the fixture's total hit counter.",
  "item": [
    {
      "name": "657.1 [EXPECT-403] a Runware task sent with deliveryMethod async under a dollar budget is refused before the call (runware-deferred)",
      "event": [
        {
          "listen": "prerequest",
          "script": {
            "type": "text/javascript",
            "exec": [
              "if (pm.variables.get('providerErrorFixture') !== '1') {",
              "  pm.execution.skipRequest();",
              "}",
              "// A run-scoped key over the fixture's runware and openai, funded by a $100 dollar budget.",
              "var BASE = pm.variables.get('baseUrl');",
              "var run = 'harness-runware-deferred-' + Date.now() + '-' + Math.floor(Math.random() * 1e9);",
              "pm.collectionVariables.set('rdbBudgetVk', 'missing');",
              "function totalHits(done) {",
              "  pm.sendRequest({ url: pm.variables.get('providerErrorFixtureUrl') + '/__hits', method: 'GET' }, function (err, res) {",
              "    var hits = (!err && res.code === 200) ? (res.json().data[0].hits || {}) : {};",
              "    var total = 0;",
              "    Object.keys(hits).forEach(function (k) { if (k.indexOf('__') !== 0) { total += hits[k]; } });",
              "    done(err, total, hits);",
              "  });",
              "}",
              "var body = { name: run, budgets: [{ max_limit: 100, reset_duration: '1h' }], provider_configs: [{ provider: 'runware', allowed_models: ['*'], key_ids: ['*'], weight: 1 }, { provider: 'openai', allowed_models: ['*'], key_ids: ['*'], weight: 1 }] };",
              "pm.sendRequest({ url: BASE + '/api/governance/virtual-keys', method: 'POST', header: { 'Content-Type': 'application/json' }, body: { mode: 'raw', raw: JSON.stringify(body) } }, function (err, res) {",
              "  pm.test('runware-deferred setup: created the budgeted key', function () {",
              "    pm.expect(err, String(err)).to.equal(null);",
              "    pm.expect(res.code, res.text()).to.eql(200);",
              "  });",
              "  var vk = res.json().virtual_key;",
              "  pm.collectionVariables.set('rdbBudgetVk', (vk.value && typeof vk.value === 'object') ? vk.value.value : vk.value);",
              "  pm.collectionVariables.set('rdbBudgetId', vk.id);",
              "  totalHits(function (err2, total) { pm.collectionVariables.set('rdbHitsBefore', String(total)); });",
              "});"
            ]
          }
        },
        {
          "listen": "test",
          "script": {
            "type": "text/javascript",
            "exec": [
              "if (pm.variables.get('providerErrorFixture') !== '1') {",
              "  pm.execution.skipRequest();",
              "}",
              "function totalHits(done) {",
              "  pm.sendRequest({ url: pm.variables.get('providerErrorFixtureUrl') + '/__hits', method: 'GET' }, function (err, res) {",
              "    var hits = (!err && res.code === 200) ? (res.json().data[0].hits || {}) : {};",
              "    var total = 0;",
              "    Object.keys(hits).forEach(function (k) { if (k.indexOf('__') !== 0) { total += hits[k]; } });",
              "    done(err, total, hits);",
              "  });",
              "}",
              "pm.test('runware-deferred: an async Runware task under a dollar budget is refused 403 policy_model_blocked (background_unsettled)', function () {",
              "  var text = pm.response.text();",
              "  pm.expect(pm.response.code, text).to.equal(403);",
              "  var j = pm.response.json();",
              "  pm.expect(j.extra_fields && j.extra_fields.error_type, text).to.equal('policy_model_blocked');",
              "  pm.expect(j.type, text).to.equal('background_unsettled');",
              "});",
              "totalHits(function (err, total, hits) {",
              "  pm.test('runware-deferred: an async Runware task under a dollar budget did not reach the upstream', function () {",
              "    pm.expect(err, String(err)).to.equal(null);",
              "    pm.expect(total, JSON.stringify(hits)).to.equal(Number(pm.collectionVariables.get('rdbHitsBefore')));",
              "  });",
              "});"
            ]
          }
        }
      ],
      "request": {
        "method": "POST",
        "header": [
          {
            "key": "Content-Type",
            "value": "application/json"
          },
          {
            "key": "x-bf-vk",
